  "interpretation": [
    "All 46 core files and all 34 optional files were enumerated. Schema rejections are unsupported coverage, not passing official tests.",
    "Coverage ratios are not OpenCode plugin compatibility rates: the official suite deliberately isolates vocabulary behavior and includes schemas outside the product subset.",
    "Validator mismatches are semantic defects within admitted schemas. Core defects occur in const/enum numeric equality (including nested values) and the mathematical integer predicate.",
    "Grammar mismatches describe one representative JSON/native spelling. A generator may legitimately require canonical numeric spelling or property order; these counts are not additional validator conformance failures.",
    "A concrete closed-loop defect exists: const -2.0 permits generation of -2, but the final validator and Qwen parser reject -2. The grammar accepts an output its own final validation rejects.",
    "Native raw-string schemas cannot encode non-string source instances. Mixed string unions may interpret raw numeric/object text as a string; five such changed round trips are excluded from native semantic comparisons.",
    "The optional ECMA regex tests expose BOM whitespace differences. Optional bignum tests also exceed the current numerical representation contract; they are kept separate from core results.",
    "Native optional newline failure tests only the selected spelling, not all permitted padding/encodings. No full native-transport impossibility claim is made."
  ],
